# Internationalization (i18n)

## Overview

This project uses `next-international` for internationalization with support for:
- **English (en)** - Default locale
- **Polish (pl)**

## Configuration Files

### Client-side Setup
```typescript
// src/locales/client.ts
'use client';

import { createI18nClient } from 'next-international/client';

export const {
  useI18n,           // Get translation function
  useScopedI18n,     // Get scoped translation function
  I18nProviderClient, // Provider component
  useCurrentLocale,  // Get current locale
  useChangeLocale,   // Change locale function
} = createI18nClient({
  en: () => import('./en'),
  pl: () => import('./pl'),
});
```

### Server-side Setup
```typescript
// src/locales/server.ts
import { createI18nServer } from 'next-international/server';

export const {
  getI18n,          // Get translation function (async)
  getScopedI18n,    // Get scoped translation function (async)
  getCurrentLocale, // Get current locale
  getStaticParams,  // For static generation
} = createI18nServer({
  en: () => import('./en'),
  pl: () => import('./pl'),
});
```

### Middleware Setup
```typescript
// middlewares/with-internationalization.ts
const I18nMiddleware = createI18nMiddleware({
  locales: ['en', 'pl'],
  defaultLocale: 'en',
});
```

## Translation File Structure

### Global Translations

Located in `src/locales/{lang}/`:

```
src/locales/
├── client.ts                 # Client-side i18n exports
├── server.ts                 # Server-side i18n exports
├── en/
│   ├── index.ts             # Aggregates all EN translations
│   ├── common.ts            # Common UI strings (buttons, pagination, etc.)
│   ├── validation.ts        # Form validation messages
│   └── routes.ts            # Navigation route labels
└── pl/
    ├── index.ts             # Aggregates all PL translations
    ├── common.ts            # Common UI strings (Polish)
    ├── validation.ts        # Validation messages (Polish)
    └── routes.ts            # Route labels (Polish)
```

### Main Locale Index

The main index file aggregates global and feature translations:

```typescript
// src/locales/en/index.ts
import auth from '@features/auth/index.client';
import inventory from '@features/inventory/index.client';
import sales from '@features/sales/index.client';
import statistics from '@features/statistics/index.client';
import warehouse from '@features/warehouse/index.client';

import common from './common';
import routes from './routes';
import validation from './validation';

export default {
  validation,
  common,
  routes,
  ...auth.locales.en,
  ...inventory.locales.en,
  ...sales.locales.en,
  ...statistics.locales.en,
  ...warehouse.locales.en,
} as const;
```

### Feature Translations

Each feature module manages its own translations in `src/features/{feature}/locales/`:

```
src/features/{feature}/
└── locales/
    ├── en/
    │   ├── index.ts         # Aggregates feature EN translations
    │   └── {feature}.ts     # Feature-specific translations
    └── pl/
        ├── index.ts         # Aggregates feature PL translations
        └── {feature}.ts     # Feature-specific translations (Polish)
```

#### Feature Locale Export Pattern

```typescript
// src/features/{feature}/locales/en/index.ts
import featureName from './feature-name';
import otherModule from './other-module';

export default {
  featureName,
  otherModule,
} as const;
```

#### Feature Client Export with Locales

```typescript
// src/features/{feature}/index.client.ts
import en from './locales/en';
import pl from './locales/pl';

export default {
  locales: {
    en,
    pl,
  },
} as const;
```

## Usage Patterns

### Server Components

```typescript
// In async server components
import { getI18n } from '@/locales/server';

export default async function ServerComponent() {
  const t = await getI18n();

  return (
    <div>
      <h1>{t('common.home.title')}</h1>
      <button>{t('common.button.submit')}</button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Client Components

```typescript
// In client components
'use client';

import { useI18n } from '@/locales/client';

export function ClientComponent() {
  const t = useI18n();

  return (
    <div>
      <h1>{t('inventory.title')}</h1>
      <button>{t('common.button.submit')}</button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Language Switching

```typescript
'use client';

import { useChangeLocale, useCurrentLocale } from '@/locales/client';

export function LanguageSwitcher() {
  const changeLocale = useChangeLocale({ preserveSearchParams: true });
  const currentLocale = useCurrentLocale();

  return (
    <button onClick={() => changeLocale(currentLocale === 'en' ? 'pl' : 'en')}>
      {currentLocale === 'en' ? 'Polski' : 'English'}
    </button>
  );
}
```

## Translation Key Patterns

### Basic Strings

```typescript
export default {
  title: 'Inventory',
  add: 'Add product',
} as const;
```

### Nested Objects

```typescript
export default {
  button: {
    submit: 'Submit',
    cancel: 'Cancel',
    loading: 'Loading...',
  },
  table: {
    name: 'Name',
    price: 'Price',
  },
} as const;
```

### Parameter Interpolation

Use `{paramName}` syntax for dynamic values:

```typescript
// Translation file
export default {
  selectedOfRows: '{count} of {total} rows selected',
  greeting: 'Hello, {name}!',
  step: 'Step {step}',
} as const;

// Usage
t('common.selectedOfRows', { count: 5, total: 10 }); // "5 of 10 rows selected"
t('common.greeting', { name: 'John' }); // "Hello, John!"
```

### Pluralization

Use `#one`, `#few`, `#other` suffixes for plural forms:

```typescript
// Translation file (supports Polish plural rules)
export default {
  dialog: {
    remove: {
      'success#one': 'Product removed successfully',
      'success#few': 'Products removed successfully',  // Polish: 2-4 items
      'success#other': 'Products removed successfully',
    },
  },
  'minLength#one': 'Minimum length is {count} character',
  'minLength#few': 'Minimum length is {count} characters',
  'minLength#other': 'Minimum length is {count} characters',
} as const;

// Usage (library selects correct form based on count)
t('inventory.dialog.remove.success', { count: 1 }); // "Product removed successfully"
t('inventory.dialog.remove.success', { count: 5 }); // "Products removed successfully"
```

**Plural suffixes:**
- `#one` - Singular (1 item)
- `#few` - Few items (Polish: 2-4, varies by language)
- `#other` - Many items (5+, or default)
- `#zero` - Zero items (optional)

## Adding New Translations

### 1. Add Global Translation

Edit `src/locales/en/common.ts` (or appropriate file):

```typescript
export default {
  // ... existing translations
  newSection: {
    title: 'New Section',
    description: 'This is a new section',
  },
} as const;
```

Then add the Polish version in `src/locales/pl/common.ts`.

### 2. Add Feature Translation

Create or edit `src/features/{feature}/locales/en/{feature}.ts`:

```typescript
export default {
  title: 'Feature Title',
  actions: {
    create: 'Create Item',
    edit: 'Edit Item',
    delete: 'Delete Item',
  },
} as const;
```

Update the feature locale index:

```typescript
// src/features/{feature}/locales/en/index.ts
import featureName from './feature-name';

export default {
  featureName,
} as const;
```

### 3. Add Validation Message

Edit `src/locales/en/validation.ts`:

```typescript
export default {
  // ... existing validations
  customValidation: 'Custom validation message',
} as const;
```

## i18n in Zod Schemas

Validation schemas use hooks to access translations:

```typescript
// schema/create-product-schema.ts
import { useI18n } from '@/locales/client';
import { z } from 'zod';

export const useCreateProductSchema = () => {
  const t = useI18n();

  return z.object({
    name: z.string().min(1, t('validation.required')),
    email: z.string().email(t('validation.email')),
    price: z.coerce.number().min(0, t('validation.positive')),
  });
};
```

## Layout Provider Setup

The i18n provider wraps the app in the locale layout:

```typescript
// src/app/[locale]/layout.tsx
import { I18nProviderClient } from '@/locales/client';

export default async function LocaleLayout({
  params,
  children,
}: {
  params: Promise<{ locale: string }>;
  children: ReactNode;
}) {
  const { locale } = await params;

  return (
    <I18nProviderClient locale={locale}>
      {children}
    </I18nProviderClient>
  );
}
```

## Best Practices

1. **Always use `as const`** on translation objects for type safety
2. **Keep translations organized** by domain (common, validation, routes, features)
3. **Use semantic keys** like `button.submit` not `submitButtonText`
4. **Add both languages** when adding new translations
5. **Use parameter interpolation** for dynamic content, not string concatenation
6. **Use pluralization** for countable items
7. **Keep feature translations in features** not in global locales
